\title{Latest Deep-Dive}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-21}
\meta{toc}{true}

\p{
    See my latest on [sigma protocols](dhsorens-004U) and [Schnorr](dhsorens-004V) — the three-move
    public-coin proof of knowledge, worked through to the one subtraction that extracts a witness
    and the simulator that is the same equation read backwards. Schnorr is where the
    [soundness notions](dhsorens-002F) I wrote up earlier were first defined, and writing it out
    fixes the naming: \em{zero-knowledge proof of knowledge} under-specifies it, since the
    zero-knowledge is only honest-verifier and \em{of knowledge} is the half carrying the content.
    Both pages sit in the [zkVMs and SNARKs](dhsorens-002C) corpus.
}
